gger in Texas I  went out to see the JFK museum it was  very well done and quite intense until  that point I really didn't know how much  JFK had done for the country back in  that era as it turns out he was  assassinated from that very window the  one on the mid ride back in 1963 or was  he there are several witnesses that have  never been shown on national TV and this  lady took film  the old rate for downstream is  to film the grassy knoll from high  elevation  and she said she saw smoke  the first one interviewer my name is  Marcos we spend a lot of years  interviewing people who traveled out of  Dallas to Amarillo and then on to  Albuquerque and rode some hot-air  balloons at dawn  and then those colorado Salalah is just  chilling out at the lodge I had an  interview with one of the non  Australians on Contiki yeah yeah okay my  name is Serena I'm 24 years old I'm from  Switzerland and  Radio Soviet and it's so much fun  what I love in Switzerland is the  mountains  as we drove out to the Grand Canyon I  began to realize that this whole  adventure was going to end pretty soon  everyone in our group was really cool  and got along extremely well our tour  guide said that our group was one of the  best he'd ever had I took a helicopter  ride over the Grand Canyon and let's  just say however big he thought the  Grand Canyon is is nothing compared to  its real size our final stop and grand  finale was none other than Las Vegas and  well let's just say whatever happens in  Vegas stays in Vegas  really but here's what I can reveal huh  Las Vegas was crazy off the charts over  the top and whatever other words you can  use to describe that vibe it had literal  palaces fitted with Greek style column  structures complete with fake skies  painted on the interior ceiling Vegas is  ridiculous it's the closest thing you'll  get to another world everything is done  to perfection and to the extreme the  interiors have fitted out with the  craziest of expensive ornaments the  ca